{"crc":"aa0293f9","kind":"Candidate","payload":{"response":"Looking at the bug report, the issue is in `lib/matplotlib/offsetbox.py` in the `_check_still_parented` method. The error occurs because `self.ref_artist.figure` can be `None` when the artist has been removed from the figure, and then trying to access `.canvas` on `None` causes the `AttributeError`.\n\nLet me examine the relevant code in the offsetbox.py file to find the exact location:\n\nThe issue is in the `DraggableBase` class (or similar) where `canvas` is defined as a property using `self.ref_artist.figure.canvas`. When `self.ref_artist.figure` is `None`, this fails.\n\nLet me search for the exact code in the file:\n\n```python\ncanvas = property(lambda self: self.ref_artist.figure.canvas)\n```\n\nThis needs to be fixed to handle the case where `self.ref_artist.figure` is `None`.\n\n# path: lib/matplotlib/offsetbox.py\n<<<<<<< SEARCH\n    ref_artist = property(lambda self: self._ref_artist)\n    canvas = property(lambda self: self.ref_artist.figure.canvas)\n=======\n    ref_artist = property(lambda self: self._ref_artist)\n    canvas = property(lambda self: self.ref_artist.figure.canvas\n                      if self.ref_artist.figure is not None else None)\n>>>>>>> REPLACE","round":1,"slot":0},"producer":{"instance":"01KZT27AVM83JW1R3R27HBB03W","kind":"drafter","parent":"01KZT27AVEQ9YXEVH4JC7NQQ36"},"schema":"Candidate@1","seq":14,"t":1786507408.71553}
{"crc":"cd6cf044","kind":"substrate.TriggerFired","payload":{"factory":"validator","firing_key":null,"input_sha256":"sha256:77c6d5c307007b2e9dae471eeadbd5cd181e8bd24b92eff5d7fe55ce0cccec97","instance":"01KZT27DAB3NPW65C7BDXQ1C6D","resolved_input":{"response":"Looking at the bug report, the issue is in `lib/matplotlib/offsetbox.py` in the `_check_still_parented` method. The error occurs because `self.ref_artist.figure` can be `None` when the artist has been removed from the figure, and then trying to access `.canvas` on `None` causes the `AttributeError`.\n\nLet me examine the relevant code in the offsetbox.py file to find the exact location:\n\nThe issue is in the `DraggableBase` class (or similar) where `canvas` is defined as a property using `self.ref_artist.figure.canvas`. When `self.ref_artist.figure` is `None`, this fails.\n\nLet me search for the exact code in the file:\n\n```python\ncanvas = property(lambda self: self.ref_artist.figure.canvas)\n```\n\nThis needs to be fixed to handle the case where `self.ref_artist.figure` is `None`.\n\n# path: lib/matplotlib/offsetbox.py\n<<<<<<< SEARCH\n    ref_artist = property(lambda self: self._ref_artist)\n    canvas = property(lambda self: self.ref_artist.figure.canvas)\n=======\n    ref_artist = property(lambda self: self._ref_artist)\n    canvas = property(lambda self: self.ref_artist.figure.canvas\n                      if self.ref_artist.figure is not None else None)\n>>>>>>> REPLACE","round":1,"slot":0},"trigger_id":"validate"},"producer":null,"schema":"substrate.TriggerFired@1","seq":15,"t":1786507408.715761}
